{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry-FEM Compatibility.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry-FEM Compatibility.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"geometry fem compatibility geometry fem compatibility","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry-FEM Compatibility.md","fileName":"Geometry-FEM Compatibility.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Geometry-FEM Compatibility","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 00:45\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CAD and FEM Geometry Exchange]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CAD and FEM Geometry Exchange","geometrycreationandimport.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry-FEM Compatibility.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry-FEM Compatibility.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"geometry fem compatibility geometry fem compatibility","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry-FEM Compatibility.md","fileName":"Geometry-FEM Compatibility.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Geometry-FEM Compatibility","heading":"Geometry-FEM Compatibility","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Geometry-FEM compatibility means that imported vertices, edges, faces, and volumes satisfy the receiving solver's requirements for connected domains, entity tolerances, dimension, and meshing. Correct CAD dimensions alone do not establish this compatibility.\n\nTiny gaps, overlapping entities, sliver faces, and incorrect junctions may be invisible in the authoring tool yet prevent continuity or create poor elements. The FEM specialist must inspect the imported topology in the host environment.","tags":["baby"],"links":["CAD and FEM Geometry Exchange","geometrycreationandimport.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry-FEM Compatibility.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry